{"authored" [{"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^{2}$ in the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-{x}^{3}}$ at $x=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-1)^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(1).\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-2x{e}^{-{x}^{3}}+3{x}^{4}{e}^{-{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =-2\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{3}}+3\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{3}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1}+3{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of $(x-1)^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2} & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}=\\frac{1}{2e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e24aad73ffb4030ea2c4e30da66080e8a81d02cd0e909da794529430e04d119" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2e}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{e}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2e}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/state.json" "file_sha256" "a11652c61554487c02161ad0cfe7a4773d9456020e1c7da47914892dd81e0e20" "basis" 1204 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030220/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}$ in the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =f(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a433e0608a9d2d23a903bc7da3e7e98dc3b0f7844bb3ffd4a203375a5292848a" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d9859227b8102038ac07c529f2318c381304674c218f4733c968b29ed0eb23" "basis" 1301 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038371/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-15639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-15639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we plug $a=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out $f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ and ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x) & ⟹ &  & f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡(x)} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{{cos}^{3}⁡(x)} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now plug the results for $f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ and ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ into our second-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =1+2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-15639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb56735993dca72d57a9dec76b0a00e06caeac0483ca4c4ab605f2d11608f2b"} {"question" "q-15639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-15639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"] ["math" "1+(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"] ["math" "1+2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"] ["math" "1+4(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"] ["math" "1+4(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-15639" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+2(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+2{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}$ in the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =f(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb56735993dca72d57a9dec76b0a00e06caeac0483ca4c4ab605f2d11608f2b"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81059" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of $(x-\\pi )^{2}$ in the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ at $x=\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =f(\\pi )+{f}^{′}(\\pi )(x-\\pi )+\\frac{{f}^{″}(\\pi )}{2}(x-\\pi )^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-\\pi )^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\pi .$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\pi )=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of $(x-\\pi )^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{″}(\\pi )}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb56735993dca72d57a9dec76b0a00e06caeac0483ca4c4ab605f2d11608f2b"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-81060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^{2}$ in the second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-{x}^{3}}$ at $x=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The second-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-1)^{2}$ in the above Taylor polynomial is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(1).\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find this coefficient, we start by computing the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-2x{e}^{-{x}^{3}}+3{x}^{4}{e}^{-{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =-2\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{3}}+3\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot {e}^{-{1}^{3}} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-1}+3{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine the coefficient of $(x-1)^{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2} & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}=\\frac{1}{2e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb56735993dca72d57a9dec76b0a00e06caeac0483ca4c4ab605f2d11608f2b"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2e"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2e}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{e}"] ["math" "\\frac{e}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-125129" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2e}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the second-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{2}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{2}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$\\,{x}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0)+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{″}(0)(x-0)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x}=(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-1} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\sqrt{2}(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4(1-\\sqrt{2}\\,x)^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ and ${f}^{″}(0)$ into our second-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =1+\\sqrt{2}\\,x+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2} \\\\  & =1+\\sqrt{2}\\,x+2\\,{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb56735993dca72d57a9dec76b0a00e06caeac0483ca4c4ab605f2d11608f2b"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a6864e6a4de96d3ab04e"} {"question" "q-347466" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063808/state.json" "file_sha256" "2ad20b42e0926f5ad1e224c66779e99a3867e18c5a43a686